  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility study for the future building of the Field Epidemiology Training and Resource Center at the National Institute of Public Health (INSP), Timor Leste</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Field Epidemiology Training and Resource Centre is a specialized professional training facility to be constructed within the National Institute of Public Health (INSP) compound in Dili, Timor-Leste, under a collaborative agreement between WHO-KOICA and the Government of Timor-Leste. Once established, it will serve as the national hub for the Field Epidemiology Training Program (FETP). It will provide a dedicated environment to train frontline health professionals in outbreak investigation, epidemiological data analysis, surveillance, risk assessment, emergency preparedness, and rapid response to public health threats.</narrative>
  </description>
